From: Tribhoon <amoapo0@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: nss: route fragments to REO2SW1 via HAL_REO1_MISC_CTL in NSS mode

In Qualcomm REO hardware architecture, fragment routing was changed
between IPQ8074 and newer SoCs (IPQ5018, QCN6122, WCN6750):
- On IPQ8074, fragment destination ring was configured in HAL_REO1_GEN_ENABLE
  bits 25:23 (HAL_REO1_GEN_ENABLE_FRAG_DST_RING).
- On IPQ5018 and QCN6122 (as on WCN6750), fragment destination ring control
  was moved to HAL_REO1_MISC_CTL (offset 0x000005d8), bits 20:17
  (HAL_REO1_MISC_CTL_FRAGMENT_DST_RING), while bits 25:23 in GEN_ENABLE
  are ignored by hardware.

Upstream ath11k defined .hal_reo1_misc_ctl = 0x000005d8 for wcn6750_regs,
but omitted it for both ipq5018_regs and qcn6122_regs (left as 0).
Because ath11k never programmed HAL_REO1_MISC_CTL on IPQ5018/QCN6122,
offset 0x05d8 remains at its power-on reset value on both radios:
  0x000c0000 = FIELD_PREP(GENMASK(20, 17), 6) -> HAL_HASH_ROUTING_RING_FW

HAL_HASH_ROUTING_RING_FW routes all fragments to Ring 19 (REO2FW), an
unserviced 64-descriptor dead-end firmware ring. In NSS offload mode,
firmware never drains Ring 19. When clients transmit 802.11 MPDU
fragments, Ring 19 fills to capacity (head 1008, tail 0) after 63
fragments, asserting global REO hardware backpressure and permanently
freezing the 5 GHz RX pipeline.

Fix this under NSS offload mode by:
1. Setting .hal_reo1_misc_ctl = 0x000005d8 in ipq5018_regs and qcn6122_regs.
2. In ath11k_hw_ipq5018_reo_setup(), under if (ab->nss.enabled), programming
   HAL_REO1_MISC_CTL with HAL_HASH_ROUTING_RING_SW1 (1). Note that we
   explicitly use the hardware ring enum HAL_HASH_ROUTING_RING_SW1 (1), which
   matches the hardware reset encoding 6 = FW and directs frames to REO2SW1
   where NSS reaps them; upstream wcn6855_reo_setup() writes
   HAL_SRNG_RING_ID_REO2SW1 (0, which selects TCL in this register).

Signed-off-by: Tribhoon <amoapo0@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/hw.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/hw.c
@@ -1104,6 +1104,12 @@ static void ath11k_hw_ipq5018_reo_setup(
 			      HAL_HASH_ROUTING_RING_SW1 << 24 |
 			      HAL_HASH_ROUTING_RING_SW1 << 28;
 
+		val = ath11k_hif_read32(ab, reo_base + HAL_REO1_MISC_CTL(ab));
+		val &= ~HAL_REO1_MISC_CTL_FRAGMENT_DST_RING;
+		val |= FIELD_PREP(HAL_REO1_MISC_CTL_FRAGMENT_DST_RING,
+				  HAL_HASH_ROUTING_RING_SW1);
+		ath11k_hif_write32(ab, reo_base + HAL_REO1_MISC_CTL(ab), val);
+
 		ath11k_hif_write32(ab, reo_base + HAL_REO1_DEST_RING_CTRL_IX_0, sw1_map);
 		ath11k_hif_write32(ab, reo_base + HAL_REO1_DEST_RING_CTRL_IX_1, sw1_map);
 		ath11k_hif_write32(ab, reo_base + HAL_REO1_DEST_RING_CTRL_IX_2, sw1_map);
@@ -3238,6 +3244,9 @@ const struct ath11k_hw_regs ipq5018_regs
 	/* WBM2SW release address */
 	.hal_wbm0_release_ring_base_lsb = 0x00000924,
 	.hal_wbm1_release_ring_base_lsb = 0x0000097c,
+
+	/* REO misc control register */
+	.hal_reo1_misc_ctl = 0x000005d8,
 };
 
 const struct ath11k_hw_hal_params ath11k_hw_hal_params_ipq5018 = {
@@ -3319,6 +3328,9 @@ const struct ath11k_hw_regs qcn6122_regs
 	/* WBM2SW release address */
 	.hal_wbm0_release_ring_base_lsb = 0x00000924,
 	.hal_wbm1_release_ring_base_lsb = 0x0000097c,
+
+	/* REO misc control register */
+	.hal_reo1_misc_ctl = 0x000005d8,
 };
 
 const struct ath11k_hw_hal_params ath11k_hw_hal_params_ipq8074 = {
